(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "adr-2609010100-the-six-apexes-are-not-six-products-of-the-same-shape")
  (:adr/title "The six apexes are not six products of the same shape, and the integration probe scores them as if they were")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-09-01")

  (:adr/context
  "Three separate attempts to close findings from ADR-2608311600 ended the same
   way: the apex was not defective, the axis was asking a question that apex
   does not have. Recorded together because one of them is an anecdote and
   three are a pattern.

   MURAKUMO, plane-reads-capability (adr-2608319900). The probe sends one token
   shape to every apex. murakumo requires an mrb_ prefix by design, so the
   probe's token never reaches the verifier and the answer does not move.
   Measured: a correctly shaped token answers 401 where the bare request
   answers 402.

   ITONAMI, four axes (adr-2608320000). The plane the probe asks,
   itonami.cloud/api/authority, answers 200 to anyone and so do the six other
   public paths in its own links map. The one credentialed plane is an MCP
   server on a workstation behind a tunnel, and its delegation layer is CACAO
   rather than Biscuit.

   ISEKAI, AOZORA, X402, controller-live. Measured 2026-09-01: auth.isekai.network
   and auth.x402.nexus do not resolve in DNS; auth.aozora.app resolves and
   answers 404. Before adding those hostnames to the shared authn Worker, the
   question is what a ceremony there would authenticate anyone INTO, and the
   three answers differ:

     aozora.app     accounts exist, but on atproto -- pds.aozora.app is a live
                    PDS with availableUserDomains [.aozora.app]. Identity here
                    is a DID and a PDS, not a passkey on the shared authn.
     x402.nexus     a catalog and settlement service. Its apex answers a service
                    index naming catalog, apply and an operator. No end-user
                    account surface.
     isekai.network an HTML application. Nothing observable from outside says
                    whether it has players with identities.

   All three apexes answer 200 on /login, /signin, /sign-in and /api/session,
   which means nothing: each is a catch-all. aozora and x402 return a
   byte-identical document for every path, isekai one document of constant
   length. The first version of this measurement read those 200s as sign-in
   surfaces.")

  (:adr/decision
  "No auth hostnames were added, and the probe was not changed.

   Adding auth.<apex> to the shared Worker for an apex with no membership behind
   it builds a ceremony that admits nobody -- the same shape as the Biscuit rung
   not written at itonami, and the same reason ADR-2608291300 kept passkey
   ceremonies off unattended routes. A green controller-live axis bought that
   way would say a person can start a ceremony, not that anyone can finish one.

   What the axes need is a per-apex answer to what the apex IS, in the table the
   probe already keeps per apex:

     which credential shape this apex accepts    (murakumo: mrb_)
     which plane is credentialed, if any         (itonami: not the public index)
     whether this apex has principals at all     (x402: apparently not)

   The probe already carries an auth host per apex. These belong beside it.

   The probe is not touched here because another session held uncommitted edits
   to it through both measurements, and is already replacing the six-character
   token and measuring several planes per apex. Two sessions editing one
   instrument is how an instrument stops being trusted.")

  (:adr/consequences
  "The headline 36.67/100 is not a fleet that is one third built. Some of its
   distance is real, some is a product shape the probe assumes and these
   surfaces do not have. Neither this ADR nor the two before it can say which
   fraction is which, because that requires the per-apex answers above, and
   those are decisions rather than measurements.

   The decisions, smallest first: does x402.nexus have end-user principals or
   only operators; is aozora's atproto identity meant to link to the Stable
   Principal or stay separate; does isekai.network have players. Each is one
   sentence from someone who knows, and each unblocks or removes an axis.

   Deliberately NOT concluded: that these apexes should have no ceremony. That
   is exactly the assertion this ADR is refusing to make from the outside.")

  (:adr/related (vector "adr-2608311600-one-auth-design-across-six-apexes"
                "adr-2608319900-credential-shape-is-per-apex-and-the-probe-reads-one-shape"
                "adr-2608320000-itonami-delegation-is-cacao-where-the-design-says-biscuit"
                "adr-2608039950-ninsho-one-authority-many-apexes"))))
